NXR-150|Bounded Cortex-M3 real-kernel IPC stress|Verification|The project shall provide a boot-static Cortex-M3 simulation port and bounded stress campaign exercising actual thread context switches, FIFO messages, semaphore handoffs, timeouts and priority-inheriting mutexes.|Host state models do not execute architecture exception entry or suspended thread stacks.|Execute QEMU MPS2 AN385 with three virtual timer timings; verify message sequence/payload conservation, token conservation, contention, low-owner priority donation, CPU-load preemption, finite deadlines and stack sentinels; fail on timeout, guest failure or missing success marker; retain logs and firmware hash.|Native C# runner, Cortex-M3 firmware link and no-heap audit, three QEMU guest runs and existing host regressions.|NXR-090,NXR-140,NXR-142|Optional RTOS_ARM_SIMULATION; arm-stress preset with SYNC, metrics, guards and round robin; one privileged Cortex-M3 with SVC/SysTick and no external IRQ dispatch.|Nine permanent 2048-byte application stacks, 1024-byte idle stack, eight-slot FIFO, fixed synchronization objects and 4096-byte exception/boot reserve; no target heap.|ports/arm-mps2/rtos_port.hpp,ports/arm-mps2/context.S,ports/arm-mps2/start.S,ports/arm-mps2/link.ld,examples/arm_stress.cpp,cmake/arm-mps2-toolchain.cmake,cmake/arm-simulation.cmake,tools/NexRT.ArmSim/Program.cs,docs/arm-stress.rst|Added a dedicated simulation BSP with a documented 72-byte integer frame and BASEPRI/SVC enqueue-and-park contract; simulation does not qualify VORAGO hardware, FPU, external IRQs or worst-case stack/latency.|ports/arm-mps2/rtos_port.hpp,ports/arm-mps2/context.S,ports/arm-mps2/start.S,examples/arm_stress.cpp,cmake/arm-simulation.cmake,tools/NexRT.ArmSim/Program.cs|examples/arm_stress.cpp,tools/NexRT.ArmSim/Program.cs|PartialSourceUnverified
